entury BCE during the reign of Pharaoh Sneferu, the founder of the Fourth Dynasty. Unlike its predecessors, the Bent Pyramid features a unique curvature, an architectural error that ultimately led to its classification as a significant transitional form between step-sided and true pyramids. This structure not only marked a bold shift in the construction techniques of Egypt but also influenced subsequent royal tomb designs throughout the Old Kingdom.

